1	/**
2	 * Cyrus mod lifecycle sweeps (docs/DOCUMENTATION.md "Cyrus mod lifecycle"). Two sweeps, both
3	 * INERT by default and each behind its own Setting (admin: /admin/cyrus-mods):
4	 *
5	 *  cyrusLifecycleSweep      Setting cyrus_lifecycle_enabled (default "false")
6	 *    1. signals: turns the Cyrus verdicts the mod-health log read stores (worker/mod-health.ts,
7	 *       plan.cyrus) into BROKEN / RECOVERED signals and tells the server owner once per break;
8	 *    2. crash loop: a Cyrus mod installed/updated in the last 20 min on a server whose game keeps
9	 *       restarting without finishing its start -> read the log since the change, and when the
10	 *       evidence pins it on that Cyrus mod, switch it off (engine "disable": the jar moves to
11	 *       /root/.nxeon-mods/disabled, config kept) and notify. Needs ENABLE_REAL_GAMEMODS=1 (or the
12	 *       sandbox); never for a mod whose disable could delete world content;
13	 *    3. auto-update: Cyrus mods the owner opted in (ServerMod.autoUpdate = AUTO) move to their
14	 *       newest finished, published, not-blocked version, only while nobody is online.
15	 *
16	 *  cyrusCompatWatchSweep    Setting cyrus_compat_watch_enabled (default "false"),
17	 *                           cyrus_compat_watch_dry_run (default "true": record + log, tell nobody)
18	 *    Creator warnings (lib/cyrus/lifecycle/creator.ts): new game version Cyrus can build for,
19	 *    servers running the mod on a newer version, errors on 2+ servers. One row per (mod, key),
20	 *    resolved when it no longer applies, in-app once + email at most 2 per creator per week
21	 *    (and only where the creator's email preference allows, kind cyrus_creator_alert).
22	 *
23	 * Every server write goes through the job queue (lib/mods/queue.ts). Never touches a server that
24	 * has a job queued or running.
25	 */
